1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:08,600
Start by slicing the vegetables thin,
then warm a little oil in the pan.

2
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:14,600
Soften the garlic gently, so it perfumes
the oil.

3
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:20,600
Add the mushrooms, onion and carrot, and
let them brown.

4
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:26,600
The udon is fresh, so it only needs hot
water.

5
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:32,600
Loosen the noodles in the water, then
drain them well.

6
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:38,600
Now the teriyaki sauce, mixed in a bowl:
soy sauce first.

7
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:44,600
Add the rice wine and brown sugar, and
stir until it dissolves.

8
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:50,600
Sear the king prawns, then grill the
secreto ibérico.

9
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:56,600
Add the noodles to the vegetables and
toss everything in the pan.

10
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:02,600
Bring back the prawns and pork, pour in
the sauce and chop some spring onion.

11
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:08,600
Keep tossing until every strand is
glossy.

12
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:14,600
Serve in a bowl with spring onion on
top. Enjoy!
